WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:01.539
Speaker 1: All right.

00:00:01.539 --> 00:00:06.650
So now we're going to wrap up the entire Trump
portion of the show.

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:11.780
This is a really important update on a story
from last week.

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:18.270
Last week, you might remember that The New
York Times is Maggie Haberman tweeted an absolutely

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:23.220
outrageous story, which was that Donald Trump
has been telling people around him that he

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:28.130
believes he's going to be reinstated to the
White House as soon as August of this year.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:32.500
Now, as a reminder, Habermann tweeted, quote,
Trump has been telling a number of people

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:36.120
he's in contact with that he expects he will
be reinstated by August.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.550
No, that isn't how it works.

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:42.940
But simply sharing the information going on
to say that it isn't happening in a vacuum.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:47.460
It is happening as he faced the possibility
of an indictment from the Manhattan district

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.200
attorney and then lastly, adding that, quote,
He is not putting out statements about the

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.460
audits in states just for the sake of it.

00:00:55.460 --> 00:01:00.329
He's been laser focused on them, according
to several people who've spoken with him,

00:01:00.329 --> 00:01:04.430
as well as Washington Post reporting a few
weeks ago.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:09.510
Now, when this story broke last week, a whole
bunch of people started immediately calling

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:11.190
it fake news.

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:18.320
And Trump's blog right before it shut down
also had a post where Donald Trump was denying

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:19.320
it.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:22.630
But since then, the story has been corroborated.

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:27.980
And the truth, as it often is with Trump,
is even crazier than the reality.

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:36.409
The right wing National Review, not a left
wing bomb throwing publication, not a publication

00:01:36.409 --> 00:01:38.390
that Trump has been calling fake news.

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:44.570
The right wing National Review published a
story called Maggie Haberman is Right, which

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:50.479
actually tells an even crazier story, reporting
that it's not only Trump who thinks he's going

00:01:50.479 --> 00:01:55.350
to be reinstated, it's Trump and two Republican
senators as well.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:02:00.780
Charles Cook writes in the piece, quote, Instead,
They should have listened because Haberman's

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:01.780
reporting was correct.

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:06.590
I can attest from speaking to an array of
different sources that Donald Trump does indeed

00:02:06.590 --> 00:02:13.099
believe quite genuinely that he, along with
former Senators David Perdue and Martha McSally,

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:20.730
will be reinstated to office this summer after
audits of the 2020 elections in Arizona, Georgia

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:22.790
and a handful of other states have been completed.

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:24.909
I can attest to that.

00:02:24.909 --> 00:02:30.079
Trump is trying hard to recruit journalists,
politicians and other influential figures

00:02:30.079 --> 00:02:36.030
to promulgate this belief not as a fundraising
tool or an infantile bit of trolling or a

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:40.329
trial balloon, but as a fact.

00:02:40.329 --> 00:02:42.040
This is nuts.

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:43.129
My friends.

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:49.310
And the article goes on to say, and remember,
this is the conservative National Review saying

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:50.310
this.

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:55.219
The article goes on to say, The scale of Trump's
delusion is quite startling.

00:02:55.219 --> 00:03:01.189
This is not merely an eccentric interpretation
of the facts or an interesting foible, nor

00:03:01.189 --> 00:03:05.349
is it an irrelevant example of anguished post
presidency chatter.

00:03:05.349 --> 00:03:10.669
It is a rejection of reality, a rejection
of law, and ultimately a rejection of the

00:03:10.669 --> 00:03:12.499
entire system of American government.

00:03:12.499 --> 00:03:16.319
There is no reinstatement clause within the
United States Constitution.

00:03:16.319 --> 00:03:21.470
Hell, there is nothing even approximating
a reinstatement clause within the United States

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:22.909
Constitution.

00:03:22.909 --> 00:03:24.920
The election has been certified.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:26.919
Joe Biden is the president.

00:03:26.919 --> 00:03:32.010
And until 2024, that is all there is to it
doesn't matter what one's view of Trump is,

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:34.669
doesn't matter whether one voted for or against
Trump.

00:03:34.669 --> 00:03:39.680
It doesn't matter whether one's view one views
Trump's role within the Republican Party favorably

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:41.400
or unfavorably.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:48.659
We are talking here about cold, hard, neutral
facts that obtain, irrespective of one's preferences.

00:03:48.659 --> 00:03:54.839
It is not too much to ask that the former
head of the executive branch should understand

00:03:54.839 --> 00:03:55.839
them.

00:03:55.839 --> 00:04:03.170
This is why I said earlier in the show a new
litmus test, a sort of a gut check, sanity

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:07.779
check question to right wingers should be
going forward.

00:04:07.779 --> 00:04:11.840
What is the soonest you believe Donald Trump
could again be?

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:15.699
President Trump says he's going to be restarting
rallies as soon as this month.

00:04:15.699 --> 00:04:21.460
Send reporters to the rallies and say to them,
sir, ma'am, what is the soonest you believe

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:22.940
Donald Trump could be president?

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:27.530
And if it's any earlier than January of twenty
twenty five, it's someone either living in

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:30.800
a fantasy world or someone very, very ignorant.

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:35.820
So not only was Maggie Haberman correct in
her reporting, not only has that been corroborated,

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:40.530
it is not Trump alone, but also David Perdue
and Martha McSally.

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:46.460
Who believe, I guess, that they're going to
be reinstated to their Senate seats somehow

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:48.009
sometime during the summer.

00:04:48.009 --> 00:04:53.520
These are really dangerous times, especially
because and we'll talk about this tomorrow

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:56.930
when this stuff inevitably doesn't happen.

00:04:56.930 --> 00:05:05.080
Will the Trump acolytes again be moved to
real world violence and destruction of property

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:10.970
and breaking and entering and trespassing
and violence that we saw on January six?

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:12.900
That's the really scary part.

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:13.840
And we'll probably talk more about that tomorrow

